  "text_pages": [
    "Visa | UTB\nVisa | UTB\nPractical Information\nUpcoming\nImportant dates\n03\nNov\nevent\nBusiness Day 2026\n06\nNov\ntbu\nOpen Day at TBU\n06\nNov\ntbu\nOpen Day at TBU\nCalendar\nFacebook\nInstagram\nTwitter\nYoutube\nVisa\nBefore you arrive\nStudents who are\nnon-EU nationals\nand have been accepted to exchange study stay at TBU in Zlín\nmust apply\nfor a long-term residence permit (for the whole year) or a visa (for the semester). Current conditions and requirements are available online at the following links:\nLong-term Student Visa\nResidence Permit for Studies\nApplicants must apply at the\npre-defined\ndiplomatic mission of the Czech Republic based on:\nA country that issued you with a travel document or which you are a national.\nIn a state in which you have been granted a long-term or permanent residence permit and have been legally residing there continuously for at least 2 years (third-country nationals living in the EU, can apply only in the\nDresden visa\ncentre\n).\nAt any of the Czech Republic’s diplomatic missions if you are a\nnational of one of these countries\n.\nThe Czech Republic does not have a diplomatic representation in every country. Some\ndiplomatic missions of the Czech Republic\nrepresent the Czech Republic in more states. Information about territorial districts\ncan be found\nhere\n.\nStudents with citizenship of EU countries\n(plus Norway, Iceland, Liechtenstein, and Switzerland)\nare exempt\nfrom visa requirements.\nExtending your visa\nYou can extend your visa in Zlín without having to leave the Czech Republic. Students are entitled to apply for an extension of a long-term visa or a long-term residence permit, on condition that their purpose of stay remains the same, at the earliest 90 days and the latest 14 days before the period of the permitted stay on the territory of the Czech Republic expires.\nA long-term residence permit issued for study at a university can be extended repeatedly. It can be extended for a maximum period of two years each time.\nMore useful information is available at the\nOfficial Information Portal for Foreigners\n.\nTravelling\nTravelling around the Schengen Area is allowed with a valid Czech long-term visa or a long-term residence permit (up to 90 days).\nVirtual tour\nFaculties and departments\nFaculty of Technology\nFaculty of Management and Economics\nFaculty of Multimedia Communications\nFaculty of Applied Informatics\nFaculty of Humanities\nFaculty of Logistics and Crisis Management\nSoučásti\nUniversity Institute\nLibrary\nHalls of Residence and Refectory\nClose\nUniverzita Tomáše Bati ve Zlíně\nYour search\nSearch\nClose"
